# Build context for container/images/ros2-iron-jammy/Dockerfile.
#
# THE CONTEXT IS THE WHOLE WORKING ROOT, WHICH CAN REACH 27 GB: scandata alone
# can be 16 GB, ros_ws 5 GB, and spatialnde2's two build directories another
# 5 GB -- none of which the image wants. So this is an ALLOWLIST: exclude everything,
# then name the handful of things the final layer installs. A denylist would
# have to be updated every time the workspace grew a new large directory, and
# the failure mode of forgetting is a multi-gigabyte context rather than an
# error anyone would notice.
*

# The dataguzzler-python side of the workspace, which the last layer installs
# system-wide with dgpy_install.sh. These total about 24 MB.
!dgpy_install.sh
!spatialnde2
!dataguzzler-python
!dgpython-param-manager
!dgpython-local
!dgpython-azurekinect
!dgpython-nidaqmx
!dgpython-uniwest
!dgpython-opencv-camera
!spatialnde2-ec-functions

# ...but not their build output. These re-exclusions come AFTER the
# re-inclusions above because later rules win, and without them spatialnde2
# alone would drag 5 GB of build/ and build-container/ into the context.
#
# .git IS DELIBERATELY KEPT, all 15 MB of it. Every one of these packages takes
# its version from setuptools_scm, which reads it from git -- so a context
# without .git installs everything as a version derived from nothing, and
# `dgpy_install.sh --check` compares that against the working tree and can no
# longer tell current from stale. The version string IS the drift detector; it
# is the whole reason the installed commit is answerable at all. 15 MB is a
# cheap price for it.
**/__pycache__
**/*.egg-info
**/*.pyc
spatialnde2/build
spatialnde2/build-container
spatialnde2-ec-functions/build
dataguzzler-python/build
